s last year – so they'll be happy to have PSG ribbons back on the trophy.Good effort from St Etienne tonight, but they came up short. Free agent Joe Hart shows off shredded physique as he hunts for a new club Bale decides NOT to play against Man City as Zidane refuses to elaborate Arsenal put Maitland-Niles for sale for £30m in desperate bid to raise cash David Silva offered £52k a week, private jet and 'elegant house' by Lazio Fraser’s Cherries walk-out backfires as Arsenal and Spurs interest dries up©News Group Newspapers Limited in England No. Loic Perrin was sent off in the 31st minute following a cynical tackle on Mbappe, who was withdrawn with an apparent ankle injury and later returned to the bench on crutches with his leg in a brace, making him a serious doubt for PSG's return to That challenge sparked a huge melee in the first competitive match in France since March, watched by a small crowd at the Stade de France, with PSG - who also lost Thilo Kehrer to injury - seeing out the win despite a spirited effort from 10-man Saint-Etienne.Denis Bouanga almost gave Claude Puel's side an early lead when he rattled the post, but it was Neymar who broke the deadlock, turning in from close range after Jessy Moulin palmed away Mbappe's strike.Moulin produced a brilliant save to deny Angel Di Maria before Perrin scythed down Mbappe as he was about to burst away, sparking unsavoury scenes as the two sets of players squared up.Referee Amaury Delerue gave the defender his marching orders following a look at the pitch-side monitor after initially showing him a yellow card and another four players were booked - including PSG substitute Marco Verratti for coming off the bench to show dissent - due to the reaction to a tackle that left Mbappe limping down the tunnel following treatment.Moulin denied Mbappe's replacement Pablo Sarabia as a second goal eluded PSG, but Neymar's early effort proved to be enough for Tuchel's men to regain the trophy.The sight of Mbappe on crutches will give Tuchel a huge headache ahead of Champions League quarter-final against Paris Saint-Germain 1-0 Saint-Etienne: Mbappe injury overshadows Coupe de France triumph Paris-Saint Germain regained the Coupe de France, but they lost Kylian Mbappe to injury in the first half.  <br>They'll be hoping those knocks aren't too bad.But it's more silverware for PSG here at the Stade de France tonight.90, Fofana BROUGHT DOWN by Silva on the edge of the penalty area.Silva looked to try and pull his leg away but it was touch and go whether he did it in time.90, Bouanga with a chance to cross from the left with men in the middle.But it's straight at Navas. <br> <br>For further details of our complaints policy and to make a complaint please click Comments are subject to our community guidelines, which can be viewed … Ready for the restart! I make that nine bookings and a … Flashback au Parc - When Fournier was hiding somewhere in the stadium First Team 13 hours ago. <br> <br>AFP . <br> Cancel online anytime. The Champions League is a matter of weeks away.PSG have won their 13th French Cup and fifth in the last six years.It's a league and cup double for Tuchel's men and they can still turn that into a treble or quadruple.It came at a cost with injuries to Mbappe and Kehrer. Tasty.A nice moment, too, as Neymar tried to whip up support from the PSG fans in the stadium.How refreshing to see actual humans in a stadium and hear real noise rather than simulations.51, Icardi has the ball in the net… but everyone had stopped as the offside flag was up.The referee waited until he scored just in case VAR wanted to overturn.But replays showed Neymar was a country mile offside.49, Handball shouts from St Etienne against Marquinhos but there's no way they're getting that.Khazri volleyed the ball at him from less than a yard away and he tried to get his arm out of the way.47, Optimistic effort from Khazri to try and catch Navas off his line after the goalkeeper's poor kick.Khazri was right o